 *
 * ─── ROUTING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The content entry src/content/products/sports-track-underlay.yaml carries
 * `path: /sports-track-underlay` (child of the `acoustic` hub). To avoid a
 * duplicate-route build error the matching branch is filtered out of
 * getStaticPaths in src/pages/[...slug].astro — the same pattern already used
 * for acoustic-underlay, zainfit, zainsquare, zainduo, zainactive-rolls and
 * curb-stone. The YAML entry stays as data (still referenced by the acoustic
 * hub nav / children list); this file serves the URL.
 *
 * ─── DECISIONS TAKEN / FLAGS (CLAUDE.md §0 "Data Integrity" + §6) ─────────
 *  - PARENT HUB: the build request's JSON-LD names the breadcrumb parent
 *    "Acoustics & Construction Systems" at /acoustics-construction-systems.
 *    That route does not exist in this project — the real acoustic hub is
 *    /acoustic-soundproofing-flooring (sports-track-underlay.yaml `hub: acoustic`,
 *    and the hub already lists this page under `children`). Both the visible
 *    breadcrumb and the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD below use the real path with the
 *    label "Acoustic & Soundproofing Flooring".
 *    TODO: confirm the intended hub label / slug with the client.
 *  - CANONICAL HOST: the request shows "rukanalzain.com"; the configured site
 *    is "ruknalzain.ae" (astro.config.mjs). Canonical is built from the
 *    configured site via BaseLayout `canonical={PATH}` (same choice as the
 *    acoustic-underlay sibling). TODO: confirm the production domain.
 *  - DESIGN SYSTEM: the request describes a neutral-950 / emerald-600 palette.
 *    The live site design system (CLAUDE.md "Brand & Visual Identity",
 *    DESIGN-NOTES.md, every sibling page) is charcoal / industrial-grey with a
 *    single amber action accent and bordered "ghost" WhatsApp buttons. This
 *    page follows the live system for cross-site consistency.
 *  - H1 / METADATA: the request's H1 ("Zain Prime — Sports Track & Court
 *    Underlay Dubai") and title/description supersede the older copy in
 *    sports-track-underlay.yaml ("…Acoustic Underlay for Sports Tracks"), the
 *    same way acoustic-underlay.astro diverged from its YAML record. The YAML
 *    stays as-is for the hub nav.
 *  - TECHNICAL SPECS: sports-track-underlay.yaml lists thickness, density and
 *    roll size as null "to collect". Every spec row rendered below was supplied
 *    in the page-build request, NOT in Rukn_Al_Zain_SEO_Content_Brief.docx.
 *    Treat as PROVISIONAL and confirm against real product test data /
 *    manufacturer certificates before go-live.
 *  - STRUCTURED DATA: a single combined @graph (BreadcrumbList + Product +
 *    FAQPage) is emitted inline. The request supplied BreadcrumbList + FAQPage;
 *    the Product node is added per CLAUDE.md §5. Organization JSON-LD is emitted
 *    sitewide by BaseLayout.
 *
 * ─── IMAGE ASSETS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * public/images/sports-track-underlay/ — intrinsic dimensions wired below to
 * prevent layout shift:
 *   - zain-prime-hero-product.jpg                    (hero, 1024×1024)
 *   - zain-prime-dramatic-problem-solution.jpg       (landscape, 1376×768)
 *   - zain-prime-technical-assembly-exploded.jpg     (landscape, 1376×768)
 *   - zain-ideal-applications-composite-dubai.jpg    (landscape, 1376×768)
 *       ↳ the request asked for three separate per-application photos
